IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-council-membership`
IMPORT `g4-council-work`

-- g4-tests-council-work.l4: tests for g4-council-work.l4 (ss.24 to 28).  Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.24 to 28
-- (inputs/law.wiki lines 198-226) before the module was run: see work/g4/expectations.md.  Each #ASSERT is one scenario; each #TRACE
-- carries its expected outcome in the `-- EXPECT` comment above it.  This module also imports g4-council-membership, to check that
-- the two modules, which write the number eleven separately, agree on it (and to prove the two import together).

§ `Tests for sections 24 to 28`

§§ `Names for the cases`

-- The eleven members, m1 being the chair.  Fields: reference | is the chair.
m1 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m1", TRUE
m2 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m2", FALSE
m3 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m3", FALSE
m4 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m4", FALSE
m5 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m5", FALSE
m6 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m6", FALSE
m7 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m7", FALSE
m8 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m8", FALSE
m9 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m9", FALSE
m10 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m10", FALSE
m11 MEANS `Serving member of the Council` OF "m11", FALSE

`all eleven serving` MEANS LIST m1, m2, m3, m4, m5, m6, m7, m8, m9, m10, m11
`ten serving, the chair among them` MEANS LIST m1, m2, m3, m4, m5, m6, m7, m8, m9, m10
`eight serving, the chair among them` MEANS LIST m1, m2, m3, m4, m5, m6, m7, m8
`six serving, the chair among them` MEANS LIST m1, m2, m3, m4, m5, m6
`five serving, the chair among them` MEANS LIST m1, m2, m3, m4, m5
`six serving, the chair not among them` MEANS LIST m2, m3, m4, m5, m6, m7
`the chair alone serving` MEANS LIST m1

-- Meetings.  Fields: serving members | every member duly summoned | present | voted for | voted against.
`a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-2 for with one abstaining` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")
`a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-3` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5", "m6")
`a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-3 and the chair for` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5", "m6")
`a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-3 and the chair against` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4"), (LIST "m1", "m5", "m6")
`a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-2, the chair and one other abstaining` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")
`a meeting of the full Council, all present, 3-2 and six abstaining` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7", "m8", "m9", "m10", "m11"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")
`a meeting of the full Council, all present, 2-2 with the chair for and five abstaining` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7", "m8", "m9", "m10", "m11"), (LIST "m1", "m2"), (LIST "m3", "m4")
`a meeting of the full Council, six present without the chair` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7"), (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4"), (LIST "m5", "m6")
`a meeting of the full Council, five present with the chair, 4-1` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4"), (LIST "m5")
`a meeting of the full Council, four present without the chair, 2-2` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5"), (LIST "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")
`a meeting of the full Council, the chair alone present` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1"), (LIST "m1"), EMPTY
`a meeting with six serving members and a seventh person present who is no member, voting` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `six serving, the chair among them`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "x1"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "x1"), (LIST "m4", "m5", "m6")
`a meeting with five serving members and a sixth person present who is no member` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `five serving, the chair among them`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "x1"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "x1"), EMPTY
`a meeting with eight serving members, five present with the chair` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `eight serving, the chair among them`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4", "m5")
`a meeting with eight serving members, four present with the chair` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `eight serving, the chair among them`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4"), (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4")
`a meeting with eight serving members, five present without the chair` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `eight serving, the chair among them`, TRUE, (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"), (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4"), (LIST "m5", "m6")
`a meeting of three present with the chair, every member summoned, 2-1` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m1", "m2"), (LIST "m3")
`a meeting of three present with the chair, not every member summoned, 2-1` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, FALSE, (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m1", "m2"), (LIST "m3")
`a meeting of three present without the chair, every member summoned, 2-1` MEANS `Meeting of the Council` OF `all eleven serving`, TRUE, (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4"), (LIST "m2", "m3"), (LIST "m4")

§§ `The number eleven`

-- Written separately in g4-council-work (restated from s.20) and in g4-council-membership (the seat list): they must agree.
#ASSERT `s 24, s 25(a) — the number of members of the Council under section 20` EQUALS `s 20 — the number of seats on the Council`
#ASSERT `s 24, s 25(a) — the number of members of the Council under section 20` EQUALS 11

§§ `Section 24: the saving of the Council's acts (eleven seats; a majority is six, the chair among them)`

#ASSERT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` `all eleven serving`
#ASSERT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` `ten serving, the chair among them`
#ASSERT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` `six serving, the chair among them`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` `five serving, the chair among them`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` `six serving, the chair not among them`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` `the chair alone serving`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` EMPTY

§§ `Section 25(a): the quorum`

-- Reading taken: a majority of the eleven seats, the chair among those present.
#ASSERT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-2 for with one abstaining`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting of the full Council, six present without the chair`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting of the full Council, five present with the chair, 4-1`
#ASSERT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting of the full Council, all present, 3-2 and six abstaining`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting of the full Council, the chair alone present`
-- A person present who is not a serving member is not a member present: five members and a stranger are not six members.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting with five serving members and a sixth person present who is no member`
#ASSERT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting with six serving members and a seventh person present who is no member, voting`
-- FORK F-base, the alternative: a majority of the members serving.  Eight serving: the quorum is five.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting with eight serving members, five present with the chair`
#ASSERT `s 25(a), alternative reading — the meeting has a quorum, a majority of the members serving being enough` `a meeting with eight serving members, five present with the chair`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), alternative reading — the meeting has a quorum, a majority of the members serving being enough` `a meeting with eight serving members, four present with the chair`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), alternative reading — the meeting has a quorum, a majority of the members serving being enough` `a meeting with eight serving members, five present without the chair`
#ASSERT `s 25(a), alternative reading — the meeting has a quorum, a majority of the members serving being enough` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-2 for with one abstaining`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), alternative reading — the meeting has a quorum, a majority of the members serving being enough` `a meeting of the full Council, five present with the chair, 4-1`

§§ `Section 25(b): decisions and the chair's casting vote`

#ASSERT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-2 for with one abstaining`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-3`
-- A tie: the chair's opinion decides.
#ASSERT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-3 and the chair for`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-3 and the chair against`
-- Those who abstain are not counted ("המשתתפים והמצביעים"): 3-2 with six abstaining carries; 2-2 with five abstaining is a tie.
#ASSERT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` `a meeting of the full Council, all present, 3-2 and six abstaining`
#ASSERT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` `a meeting of the full Council, all present, 2-2 with the chair for and five abstaining`
-- A tie in which the chair cast no vote: the text does not answer (a named refusal, never FALSE).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-2, the chair and one other abstaining` BECAUSE "s 25(b) gives the casting vote to the chair's opinion; the votes are equal and the chair cast none, which the text does not answer"
-- FORK F-25b-tie, the alternative: a tie in which the chair cast no vote fails the proposal.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(b), alternative reading — a tie in which the chair cast no vote fails the proposal, at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-2, the chair and one other abstaining`
#ASSERT `s 25(b), alternative reading — a tie in which the chair cast no vote fails the proposal, at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-3 and the chair for`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(b), alternative reading — a tie in which the chair cast no vote fails the proposal, at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-3 and the chair against`
#ASSERT `s 25(b), alternative reading — a tie in which the chair cast no vote fails the proposal, at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-2 for with one abstaining`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(b), alternative reading — a tie in which the chair cast no vote fails the proposal, at` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-3`

-- Only serving members present count as voters: the stranger's vote is not counted, so 2-3, not a 3-3 tie decided by the chair.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` `a meeting with six serving members and a seventh person present who is no member, voting`

-- A decision needs the quorum as well.
#ASSERT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-2 for with one abstaining`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-3`
#ASSERT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-3 and the chair for`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-3 and the chair against`
-- Five present with the chair, 4-1: a lopsided vote without a quorum carries nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of the full Council, five present with the chair, 4-1`
-- No quorum and a tie with no chair: FALSE, not a refusal, because the quorum fails first.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of the full Council, four present without the chair, 2-2`
-- Quorum and a tie with no chair vote: the refusal is reached.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-2, the chair and one other abstaining`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of the full Council, the chair alone present`

§§ `Section 25(c): deliberation in an incomplete composition (trap T28)`

#ASSERT `s 25(c) — the Council may deliberate in an incomplete composition` `a meeting of three present with the chair, every member summoned, 2-1`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(c) — the Council may deliberate in an incomplete composition` `a meeting of three present with the chair, not every member summoned, 2-1`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(c) — the Council may deliberate in an incomplete composition` `a meeting of three present without the chair, every member summoned, 2-1`
-- Reading A: the meeting that may deliberate has no quorum, so it carries no decision.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting of three present with the chair, every member summoned, 2-1`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` `a meeting of three present with the chair, every member summoned, 2-1`
-- CONTRADICTION C-25 ("its members" in (a) and in (c)): eight serving, three seats vacant, every serving member summoned, the chair and four others present.
-- (c): all its members were summoned (read as the serving ones: a vacant seat has no member to summon), so the Council may deliberate; (a) on the eleven: no quorum;
-- (a) on the members serving: a quorum.  The same phrase cannot mean the eleven in (a) and the serving in (c) without a reading being chosen.
#ASSERT `s 25(c) — the Council may deliberate in an incomplete composition` `a meeting with eight serving members, five present with the chair`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` `a meeting with eight serving members, five present with the chair`
#ASSERT `s 25(a), alternative reading — the meeting has a quorum, a majority of the members serving being enough` `a meeting with eight serving members, five present with the chair`

-- FORK F-T28, reading B: (c) relaxes (a): the same meeting carries its 2-1.
#ASSERT `s 25(c), alternative reading — the Council's decision is carried at a meeting held in an incomplete composition` `a meeting of three present with the chair, every member summoned, 2-1`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(c), alternative reading — the Council's decision is carried at a meeting held in an incomplete composition` `a meeting of three present with the chair, not every member summoned, 2-1`
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(c), alternative reading — the Council's decision is carried at a meeting held in an incomplete composition` `a meeting of three present without the chair, every member summoned, 2-1`

§§ `Sections 25(d) and 25(e)`

-- A MAY: using an adviser who can help is permitted and the permission left unused breaches nothing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 25(d) — the Council may use advisers and experts who can help form its position` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `use an adviser or an expert to help form the Council's position` `the Council` "an engineer" TRUE AT 5

-- An adviser who cannot help is not within the permission.
-- EXPECT STANDING use an adviser or an expert to help form the Council's position
#TRACE `s 25(d) — the Council may use advisers and experts who can help form its position` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `use an adviser or an expert to help form the Council's position` `the Council` "an engineer" FALSE AT 5

-- EXPECT STANDING use an adviser or an expert to help form the Council's position
#TRACE `s 25(d) — the Council may use advisers and experts who can help form its position` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)

-- (e): where the Law has fixed the matter the Council has nothing to fix; otherwise it must fix its methods.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 25(e) — the Council must fix its working methods and procedures where the Law has not` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)

-- EXPECT STANDING fix the Council's working methods and procedures
#TRACE `s 25(e) — the Council must fix its working methods and procedures where the Law has not` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 25(e) — the Council must fix its working methods and procedures where the Law has not` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `fix the Council's working methods and procedures` `the Council` AT 40

§§ `Section 26(a): the functions`

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(a)(1) — the Council must advise the Minister on exempting classes of work on cooling systems from the licence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `advise the Minister on exempting classes of work from the licence` `the Council` AT 10

-- No time is stated, so the duty stands and no breach is recorded however long it waits.
-- EXPECT STANDING advise the Minister on exempting classes of work from the licence
#TRACE `s 26(a)(1) — the Council must advise the Minister on exempting classes of work on cooling systems from the licence` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5000)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(a)(2) — the Council must advise the Registrar on the Ministry's policy` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `advise the Registrar on the Ministry's policy` `the Council` AT 10

-- EXPECT STANDING advise the Registrar on the Ministry's policy
#TRACE `s 26(a)(2) — the Council must advise the Registrar on the Ministry's policy` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5000)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(a)(3) — the Council must advise the Registrar on an individual application or decision` "application 17" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `advise the Registrar on an individual application or decision` `the Council` "application 17" AT 10

-- Advice on a different application does not discharge the duty for this one.
-- EXPECT STANDING advise the Registrar on an individual application or decision
#TRACE `s 26(a)(3) — the Council must advise the Registrar on an individual application or decision` "application 17" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `advise the Registrar on an individual application or decision` `the Council` "application 18" AT 10

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(a)(4) — the Council must perform any other function the Law gives it` "advise under section 17(c)" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `perform another function the Law gives the Council` `the Council` "advise under section 17(c)" AT 10

-- EXPECT STANDING perform another function the Law gives the Council
#TRACE `s 26(a)(4) — the Council must perform any other function the Law gives it` "advise under section 17(c)" AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5000)

-- FORK F-26a, the alternative: the functions are powers; an unused power breaches nothing and is still standing.
-- EXPECT STANDING advise the Minister on exempting classes of work from the licence
#TRACE `s 26(a), alternative reading — the Council may perform the function` `function (1): advising the Minister on exemption from licensing` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5000)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(a), alternative reading — the Council may perform the function` `function (2): advising the Registrar on the Ministry's policy` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `advise the Registrar on the Ministry's policy` `the Council` AT 10

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(a), alternative reading — the Council may perform the function` `function (4): any other function the Law gives the Council` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `perform another function the Law gives the Council` `the Council` "advise under section 17(c)" AT 10

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(a), alternative reading — the Council may perform the function` `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `advise the Registrar on an individual application or decision` `the Council` "application 17" AT 10

§§ `Section 26(b): subcommittees and delegation`

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(b) — the Council may appoint a subcommittee, from its members or from outside, to advise it` "the licensing subcommittee" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `appoint a subcommittee to advise the Council` `the Council` "the licensing subcommittee" AT 10

-- Delegation is available for the function of s.26(a)(3) only.
#ASSERT `s 26(b) — the Council may delegate its powers in the function to a subcommittee` `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(b) — the Council may delegate its powers in the function to a subcommittee` `function (1): advising the Minister on exemption from licensing`
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(b) — the Council may delegate its powers in the function to a subcommittee` `function (2): advising the Registrar on the Ministry's policy`
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(b) — the Council may delegate its powers in the function to a subcommittee` `function (4): any other function the Law gives the Council`

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(b) — the Council's power to delegate its powers in the function to the subcommittee` `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions` "the licensing subcommittee" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council` DOES `delegate the Council's powers in the function of section 26(a)(3) to a subcommittee` `the Council` "the licensing subcommittee" AT 10

-- EXPECT STANDING delegate the Council's powers in the function of section 26(a)(3) to a subcommittee
#TRACE `s 26(b) — the Council's power to delegate its powers in the function to the subcommittee` `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions` "the licensing subcommittee" AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5000)

-- For the function of (2) there is no power to delegate: nothing stands.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 26(b) — the Council's power to delegate its powers in the function to the subcommittee` `function (2): advising the Registrar on the Ministry's policy` "the licensing subcommittee" AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5000)

§§ `Sections 24 to 26: whether the Council was consulted and its advice validly given (IP7)`

-- Sources of advice.
`advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it` MEANS `the Council at a meeting` OF `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 3-2 for with one abstaining`
`advice formed at a meeting without a quorum` MEANS `the Council at a meeting` OF `a meeting of the full Council, five present with the chair, 4-1`
`advice formed at a quorate meeting that did not carry it` MEANS `the Council at a meeting` OF `a meeting of the full Council, six present with the chair, 2-3`
`advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, procedure followed` MEANS `a subcommittee that advises the Council` OF TRUE, (JUST TRUE)
`advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, procedure not followed` MEANS `a subcommittee that advises the Council` OF TRUE, (JUST FALSE)
`advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, no procedure fixed` MEANS `a subcommittee that advises the Council` OF TRUE, NOTHING
`advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated nothing, procedure followed` MEANS `a subcommittee that advises the Council` OF FALSE, (JUST TRUE)
`advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated nothing, no procedure fixed` MEANS `a subcommittee that advises the Council` OF FALSE, NOTHING

-- Functions, by item.
function1 MEANS `function (1): advising the Minister on exemption from licensing`
function2 MEANS `function (2): advising the Registrar on the Ministry's policy`
function3 MEANS `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions`
function4 MEANS `function (4): any other function the Law gives the Council`

-- Consultations.  Fields: the function | a request was made | the source of the advice, if any.
`a consultation under (3), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST `advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`)
`a consultation under (1), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function1, TRUE, (JUST `advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`)
`a consultation under (2), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function2, TRUE, (JUST `advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`)
`a consultation under (4), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function4, TRUE, (JUST `advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`)
`a consultation under (3), advice formed at a meeting without a quorum` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST `advice formed at a meeting without a quorum`)
`a consultation under (3), advice formed at a quorate meeting that did not carry it` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST `advice formed at a quorate meeting that did not carry it`)
`a consultation under (3), a subcommittee that followed the procedure` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, procedure followed`)
`a consultation under (3), a subcommittee that did not follow the procedure` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, procedure not followed`)
`a consultation under (3), a subcommittee, no procedure fixed` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, no procedure fixed`)
`a consultation under (3), a subcommittee with no delegation, procedure followed` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated nothing, procedure followed`)
`a consultation under (3), a subcommittee with no delegation, no procedure fixed` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated nothing, no procedure fixed`)
`a consultation under (2), a subcommittee that followed the procedure` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function2, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, procedure followed`)
`a consultation under (2), a subcommittee, no procedure fixed` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function2, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, no procedure fixed`)
`a consultation under (1), a subcommittee that followed the procedure` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function1, TRUE, (JUST `advice of a subcommittee to which the Council delegated its powers, procedure followed`)
`a consultation under (3) in which no advice has been given yet` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, TRUE, NOTHING
`a consultation under (3) in which no request was made, though advice exists` MEANS `Consultation of the Council` OF function3, FALSE, (JUST `advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`)

-- The Council was consulted: a request was made.
#ASSERT `s 26 — the Council was consulted` `a consultation under (3), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`
#ASSERT `s 26 — the Council was consulted` `a consultation under (3) in which no advice has been given yet`
#ASSERT NOT `s 26 — the Council was consulted` `a consultation under (3) in which no request was made, though advice exists`

-- The Council's own decision, whichever function.
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (1), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (2), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (4), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3), advice formed at a meeting without a quorum`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3), advice formed at a quorate meeting that did not carry it`
-- No advice yet, or no request: not validly given.
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3) in which no advice has been given yet`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3) in which no request was made, though advice exists`
-- A subcommittee's advice: valid only for function (3), only if delegated, and only if it followed the Council's procedure.
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3), a subcommittee that followed the procedure`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3), a subcommittee that did not follow the procedure`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3), a subcommittee with no delegation, procedure followed`
-- Function (2) and function (1): a subcommittee does not give the Council's advice, delegated or not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (2), a subcommittee that followed the procedure`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (1), a subcommittee that followed the procedure`
-- No procedure fixed by the Council: where it matters the text does not answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3), a subcommittee, no procedure fixed`
-- It does not matter where the answer is already FALSE: no delegation, or the wrong function, decides first.
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (3), a subcommittee with no delegation, no procedure fixed`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26 — the Council's advice was validly given` `a consultation under (2), a subcommittee, no procedure fixed`

-- FORK F-26-sub, the alternative: a subcommittee's delegated advice suffices for every function.
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26, alternative reading — the Council's advice was validly given, a subcommittee's delegated advice sufficing for every function` `a consultation under (2), a subcommittee that followed the procedure`
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26, alternative reading — the Council's advice was validly given, a subcommittee's delegated advice sufficing for every function` `a consultation under (1), a subcommittee that followed the procedure`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 to 26, alternative reading — the Council's advice was validly given, a subcommittee's delegated advice sufficing for every function` `a consultation under (3), a subcommittee with no delegation, procedure followed`
#ASSERT `s 24 to 26, alternative reading — the Council's advice was validly given, a subcommittee's delegated advice sufficing for every function` `a consultation under (3), advice formed at a quorate meeting that carried it`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 24 to 26, alternative reading — the Council's advice was validly given, a subcommittee's delegated advice sufficing for every function` `a consultation under (2), a subcommittee, no procedure fixed`

§§ `Section 27: remuneration and expenses`

-- Fields: a State employee | an employee of a budgeted body | an employee of a supported body | an employee of the body represented.
`a member who is nobody's employee`                         MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a State employee`                                          MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an employee of a budgeted body`                            MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`an employee of a supported body, not of the body represented` MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`an employee of a supported body that is the body represented` MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`an employee of a private body that is the body represented`  MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a State employee who is also an employee of the body represented` MEANS `Employment of a member of the Council` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` `a member who is nobody's employee`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` `a State employee`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` `an employee of a budgeted body`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` `an employee of a supported body that is the body represented`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` `a State employee who is also an employee of the body represented`
-- The supported-body employee who does not work for the body represented: (a) does not entitle him, (b) does not deny him: no answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` `an employee of a supported body, not of the body represented`
-- CONTRADICTION C-27, the discriminating case: a private-body employee working for the body he represents.  (a) entitles, (b) denies.
#ASSERT `s 27(a) — the member is not a State, budgeted-body or supported-body employee` `an employee of a private body that is the body represented`
#ASSERT `s 27(b) — the member is a State employee, a budgeted-body employee or an employee of the body the member represents` `an employee of a private body that is the body represented`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` `an employee of a private body that is the body represented`
#ASSERT `s 27, alternative reading — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses, section 27(a) prevailing` `an employee of a private body that is the body represented`
-- The two readings agree elsewhere.
#ASSERT `s 27, alternative reading — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses, section 27(a) prevailing` `a member who is nobody's employee`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27, alternative reading — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses, section 27(a) prevailing` `a State employee`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27, alternative reading — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses, section 27(a) prevailing` `an employee of a budgeted body`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27, alternative reading — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses, section 27(a) prevailing` `an employee of a supported body, not of the body represented`
-- Payment from the Ministry: not for a member of the (a) class; silent for the rest.
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(a) — the member is entitled to payment from the Ministry for taking part in meetings` `a member who is nobody's employee`
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(a) — the member is entitled to payment from the Ministry for taking part in meetings` `an employee of a private body that is the body represented`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(a) — the member is entitled to payment from the Ministry for taking part in meetings` `a State employee`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 27(a) — the member is entitled to payment from the Ministry for taking part in meetings` `an employee of a supported body, not of the body represented`

§§ `Section 28: the status equation`

-- Fields of the call: the member's employment, the enactment, an act in the Council, a provision the item names.
`the Gifts Law` MEANS `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979`
`the Penal Law item` MEANS `the Penal Law, the provisions concerning public servants`
`the Restrictions after Retirement Law` MEANS `the Public Service (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969`
`the Party Activity Law item` MEANS `the Civil Service (Restriction of Party Activity and Fund-raising) Law 1959, the provisions on all State employees`
`the Evidence Ordinance item` MEANS `the Evidence Ordinance, the provisions on a public servant's certificate`
`the Elections Law` MEANS `the Knesset Elections Law`

#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Gifts Law` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Restrictions after Retirement Law` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Elections Law` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
-- Items 2, 4 and 5 only for the provisions they name.
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Penal Law item` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Penal Law item` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Party Activity Law item` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Party Activity Law item` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Evidence Ordinance item` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Evidence Ordinance item` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
-- Reading A: only the member's acts in the Council.
#ASSERT NOT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Gifts Law` `for an act in the Council being` FALSE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Elections Law` `for an act in the Council being` FALSE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
-- FORK F-28-scope, reading B: the listed enactment, whatever the act.
#ASSERT `s 28, alternative reading — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Gifts Law` `whatever the act, a provision the item names being` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28, alternative reading — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Penal Law item` `whatever the act, a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 28, alternative reading — the member with the employment` `a member who is nobody's employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Penal Law item` `whatever the act, a provision the item names being` FALSE
-- A State employee is one already, whatever the act.
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` `a State employee` `is treated as a State employee under` `the Gifts Law` `for an act in the Council being` FALSE `and a provision the item names being` FALSE
